2. Use a shared queue or list of files to process
3. Use a mutex per file (or a hash map of mutexes) to ensure only one thread processes a specific file at a time
4. Use a global mutex to protect the file list/queue
5. Worker threads pick files from the queue, lock the specific file, process it, unlock, mark as done

